---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { tagline } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Bill Beacham: veteran design director, BAFTA game design juror, and tabletop games master based in London.">
  <PageHead
    title="About<br><span>me</span>"
    lede={tagline}
    focus="85% 55%"
  />

  <section class="about">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        My name is Bill Beacham. I have 30 years experience in making games, involving some of the biggest and best—loved IPs in film, comics and gaming, including <i>James Bond</i>, <i>Batman</i>, <i>Tomb Raider</i>, <i>Deus Ex</i>, <i>Just Cause</i> 
        and <i>Life is Strange</i>. Games which have won countless awards, been enjoyed by tens of millions of players and generated 100s of millions of 
        dollars in revenue.
      </p>
      <p>
        I specialize in immersive experiences where every part of the creative design is dedicated to delivering a particular gameplay fantasy.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have worked in multiple genres and business models, which has given me a deep understanding of a huge range of mechanics and systems. 
        I have worked with teams throughout Europe, the US and Japan, including co-development and outsource partners.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have worked on franchise plans for long-running series with Just Cause and Life is Strange, 
        evolving the player experience without losing sight of what made the games popular in the first place.
      </p>
      <p>
        My speciality is shaping and refining creative visions: giving clear, actionable direction to development teams; 
        aligning design, narrative, art, audio and technology; and keeping a project the right size for its time and budget.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have led teams to deliver my own game designs, and I have decades of experience in supporting Game Directors and creative leads in realizing their visions. I love helping people make games. 
        I am known for collaborative problem-solving, clear communication and advocating for player immersion, motivation and emotional impact.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have a huge wealth of experience, knowledge and passion. I am currently looking for the perfect way to make use of them going forward.
      </p>
      <h2>Beyond the studio</h2>
      <p>
        I run long tabletop campaigns online and in person, mostly recently Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5e, World of Darkness, and various indie Powered by the Apocalypse 
         games. I’m writing my won adventures for publication, and about to start professional GMing in my spare time. 
        I’ve served as a game design juror for BAFTA, and studied Philosophy at the University of Nottingham.
             </p>
      <h2>Working together</h2>
      <p>
        I’m open to design direction roles and to consulting: pitch and concept reviews, milestone
        and content feedback, establishing or evolving franchise pillars, and building & managing design teams.
        <a href="mailto:bill.beacham@gmail.com">Email me</a> or find me on
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bill-beacham">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside aria-label="At a glance">
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Based</dt><dd>London</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Open to</dt><dd>Design direction roles and consulting</dd></div>
        <div><dt>In games since</dt><dd>1997</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Studios</dt><dd>Eurocom, Eidos, Square Enix</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Juror</dt><dd>BAFTA, game design</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Studied</dt><dd>Philosophy, University of Nottingham</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px) var(--gutter);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(240px, 22rem);
    gap: 48px clamp(40px, 7vw, 120px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  aside { position: sticky; top: 24px; border-top: var(--rule); }
  aside div { padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 30%, transparent); }
  dt { font: 700 1rem/1 var(--display); letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rust); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  dd { margin: 0; font: 700 1.5rem/1.1 var(--display); text-transform: uppercase; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } aside { position: static; } }
  .lead { font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.4; }
</style>
